Subject: [PATCH 11164/11362] [outer-loop] The diversity arm can only fire once
 per run

Verified in source before recording. force_exploration_diversity is guarded by
not diversity_active, which reads explorer._hybrid_diversity. That flag is set
at init and set True when the arm fires, and no line anywhere sets it back to
False. The supervisor clears _arms_used on every level-up, so the table thinks
the arm is available again while the explorer state says it is not.

The arm therefore fires once per RUN inside a table designed to reset per
level, and every level after the first runs with fewer rungs than the table
advertises. Every deep level in the corpus is missing that arm.

That is the mechanism behind the whole confusion: it is why deep levels never
satisfy 'every enabled arm fired', and why a per-level arms_fired fix would
suppress the genuinely exhausted levels instead of surfacing them.

The reviewer withdrew its own proposed fix after measuring it a no-op, and
answered the open question: not per-level configured, per-level reachable.

Correcting my own framing rather than the subagent's work. Under the honest
strict form, zero cells qualify on the current corpus, because
stagnations_unredirected is a run-level scalar with no level attribution and no
entry carries window rows yet. So '64 unredirected stagnations is the written
specification for a new arm', which I recorded and briefed round two on as its
highest-value thread, is weaker than it looked. The 64 is real; its attribution
to an exhausted level is not yet evidenced.

Recommending the once-per-run arm be fixed first, independently of the cell
condition. Merge still not advised.

